From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Saphira forward-port <builder@saphira.vm2.uk>
Date: Thu, 9 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [FWD 7.2.9] mm/damon: skip private node memory

Fwd-port of upstream ("mm/damon: skip private node memory in DAMON
migration and pageout", Gregory Price, series position 027) onto Linux
7.2.9.

Why needed: 7.2.9 DAMON evolved (node_stat_add_folio accounting in
the migrate path and shifted surroundings); only the migrate hunk
needed context refresh, keeping the guard in the same position
(after filter accounting, before LRU isolation). Include + pageout
hunks verbatim upstream.

Byte-identical upstream patch retained in series/ (recorded SKIP-FWD).
Verifies with git apply --check (no fuzz).

Signed-off-by: Saphira builder <builder@saphira.vm2.uk>
---
diff --git a/mm/damon/paddr.c b/mm/damon/paddr.c
index b3507b1f6..8b0599508 100644
--- a/mm/damon/paddr.c
+++ b/mm/damon/paddr.c
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
 #include <linux/swap.h>
 #include <linux/memory-tiers.h>
 #include <linux/mm_inline.h>
+#include <linux/node_private.h>
 
 #include "../internal.h"
 #include "ops-common.h"
@@ -242,6 +243,10 @@ static unsigned long damon_pa_pageout(struct damon_region *r,
 			continue;
 		}
 
+		/* private node memory is not reclaimable by default */
+		if (folio_is_private_node(folio))
+			goto put_folio;
+
 		if (damos_pa_filter_out(s, folio))
 			goto put_folio;
 		else
@@ -336,6 +341,10 @@ static unsigned long damon_pa_migrate(struct damon_region *r,
 		else
 			*sz_filter_passed += folio_size(folio) / addr_unit;
 
+		/* private nodes do not support migration by default */
+		if (folio_is_private_node(folio))
+			goto put_folio;
+
 		if (!folio_isolate_lru(folio))
 			goto put_folio;
 		node_stat_add_folio(folio, NR_ISOLATED_ANON +
--
